  - Id: tool.cell-selector
    Kingdom: 3
    DisplayName: Cell Selector
    Tagline: The freestyle world picker - and the freestyle reset. Fly through for
      a matrix of mini-cells; fly a mini-cell to become that world. Fly the one you
      are already in to reset it.
    Description: 
    Image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 402274b84242e2c419babc61c86c58fc, type: 3}
    SourcePrefab: {fileID: 0}
    SourceConfig: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2d94c7a6f81e4b53ae67d0925cf3b8a1, type: 2}
    AccentColor: {r: 0.55, g: 0.75, b: 1, a: 1}
    UnlockedByDefault: 1
    DiscoveryKey: use.tool.cell-selector
    PreviewYaw: -28
    PreviewPitch: 16
    PreviewPadding: 1.05
    FlatSilhouette: 0
    Group: "2 \xB7 World"
    SortOrder: 0
    LockAutoHarvest: 0
    Stats:
    - Label: Kind
      Value: "World \u2014 it changes WHERE YOU ARE. A world arrives or leaves, which
        is the heaviest thing any tool does"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Activation
      Value: "Fly your vessel through its ring \u2014 the ring IS the trigger volume,
        drawn at its own radius, so what you can see is what you can cross"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Objective
      Value: "None. A tool has no score, no end condition and nothing on a clock
        \u2014 it is a thing to play with for as long as you like"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: In your toybox
      Value: "Yes \u2014 unlocked from the start"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Found at
      Value: "Out by the cell membrane, at 300\xB0 around the cell"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Form
      Value: "One station that opens into a matrix of mini-cells \u2014 each a real
        scale model of the world it builds, sampled from that world's own generator"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Offers
      Value: "Every world the cell you are in can be \u2014 the tool reads the cell's
        own list rather than keeping a second one"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: The swap
      Value: The old world suctions away and the chosen one grows back behind a veil.
        Nothing pops in or out
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Also the reset
      Value: "Pick the world you are already in and you get the same cycle on the
        same config \u2014 the accumulated freestyle trail goes with it"
      Authored: 0
    Variants: []
  - Id: tool.conveyor
    Kingdom: 3
    DisplayName: Wanderway
    Tagline: Fly through to summon an endless trail of little worlds.
    Description: 
    Image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 44b9c6faf238c4041b0573026a9cf203, type: 3}
    SourcePrefab: {fileID: 0}
    SourceConfig: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3c1bc1b829fa4f7ea2c153842659d24d, type: 2}
    AccentColor: {r: 0.11635202, g: 0.22510868, b: 1, a: 1}
    UnlockedByDefault: 1
    DiscoveryKey: use.tool.conveyor
    PreviewYaw: -28
    PreviewPitch: 16
    PreviewPadding: 1.05
    FlatSilhouette: 0
    Group: "2 \xB7 World"
    SortOrder: 0
    LockAutoHarvest: 0
    Stats:
    - Label: Kind
      Value: "World \u2014 it changes WHERE YOU ARE. A world arrives or leaves, which
        is the heaviest thing any tool does"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Activation
      Value: "Fly your vessel through its ring \u2014 the ring IS the trigger volume,
        drawn at its own radius, so what you can see is what you can cross"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Objective
      Value: "None. A tool has no score, no end condition and nothing on a clock
        \u2014 it is a thing to play with for as long as you like"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: In your toybox
      Value: "Yes \u2014 unlocked from the start"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Found at
      Value: "Out by the cell membrane, at 60\xB0 around the cell"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Form
      Value: "A run you leave for and come back from \u2014 not a matrix. Fly it
        once to go, and the return station rides the end of your own trail"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: What happens
      Value: The cell is handed its bare canvas and a field of little worlds streams
        ahead of you, wherever you fly, for as long as you fly
      Authored: 0
    - Label: The belt
      Value: "20 scenes of 1,500 prisms \u2014 30,000 in all, built once and then
        transported forever. The scene farthest behind you is the one that blooms
        ahead"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Tether
      Value: 100 prisms. Your trail follows you rather than accumulating, and the
        way home is always one tether-length behind
      Authored: 0
    - Label: You will find
      Value: Structures, skimmable crystals, and flora and fauna released into the
        cell as ordinary citizens
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Getting back
      Value: 'Three ways, all the same thing: the return station, another pass through
        the tool, or leaving freestyle'
      Authored: 0
    Variants: []
  - Id: tool.painting
    Kingdom: 3
    DisplayName: Connect the Dots
    Tagline: Connect the dots to paint 3D masterpieces with your trail.
    Description: 
    Image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1799a448ed70b634ba47d70d141bb90e, type: 3}
    SourcePrefab: {fileID: 0}
    SourceConfig: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8ebb1b53a0d3784f94f1f72bbacdbe1, type: 2}
    AccentColor: {r: 0.2, g: 0.9, b: 1, a: 1}
    UnlockedByDefault: 1
    DiscoveryKey: use.tool.painting
    PreviewYaw: -28
    PreviewPitch: 16
    PreviewPadding: 1.05
    FlatSilhouette: 0
    Group: "3 \xB7 Creation"
    SortOrder: 0
    LockAutoHarvest: 0
    Stats:
    - Label: Kind
      Value: "Creation \u2014 it LEAVES SOMETHING BEHIND that lives on without you:
        conserved mass, or a population"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Activation
      Value: "Fly your vessel through its ring \u2014 the ring IS the trigger volume,
        drawn at its own radius, so what you can see is what you can cross"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Objective
      Value: "None. A tool has no score, no end condition and nothing on a clock
        \u2014 it is a thing to play with for as long as you like"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: In your toybox
      Value: "Yes \u2014 unlocked from the start"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Found at
      Value: "Out by the cell membrane, at 0\xB0 around the cell"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Form
      Value: "One station that opens into a gallery \u2014 fly a painting to start
        it"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Offers
      Value: 16 paintings
      Authored: 0
    - Label: How you paint
      Value: Your own trail is the brush. Fly the dots in order; the gates recolour
        your trail between strokes and lift the pen between them
      Authored: 0
    - Label: The marks
      Value: Cones point at where you go next and mean the trail is ON; jacks end
        a stroke and mean it is OFF
      Authored: 0
    - Label: Progress
      Value: "Saved. A half-finished painting survives a vessel swap, a game and
        a session \u2014 the prisms you already drew grow back with it"
      Authored: 0
    - Label: When it is done
      Value: Share it as a page you can spin, or repaint it
      Authored: 0
